>While we're on this subject, does anybody actually like the model
>where certain monsters want a +x or better weapon before they
>condescend to take damage?

I don't think it even makes sense! For two reasons:

1) In NetHack, enchantment, despite its name, does _not_ imply magical
enhancement. (For example, dulling a blade by engraving gives it a
negative enchantment. And I think those cavemen with +2 slings owe
their weapon's quality to fine workmanship more than something like
dweomercraft.)

2) The above point regardless, if _only_ the magical component of a
weapon does damage to said enemy, shouldn't the physical component
(i.e, the strength of the wielder, the sharpness of the blade) be
subtracted from the damage calculation?



